<title>FINLAND: SPONSOR JAN-AUG PROFIT FIM 48 MLN VS 85 MLN.</title>
<headline>SPONSOR JAN-AUG PROFIT FIM 48 MLN VS 85 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eight months to Aug 31,</p>
<p>					   (million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items			  48.4 vs 85.3</p>
<p> Net sales					  694.7 vs 2,526.0</p>
<p> Operating profit				  48.4 vs 98.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Finnish holding company is Sponsor Oy.</p>
<p>Sponsor is fully-owned subsidiary of Merita Bank .</p>
<p> Operating profit before depreciation	75.4 vs 151.9</p>
<p> Net financial items				nil vs 13.4 charge</p>
<p> Extraordinary items				nil vs nil</p>
<p> Minorities				  charge 6.6 vs 6.0 charge</p>
<p> Profit before appropriations, taxes	 41.8 vs 79.3</p>
<p> Equity to assets ratio (percent)	    68.6 vs 36.0</p>
<p>NOTE - The figures for January-August 1995 include trading</p>
<p>house Kaukomarkkinat Oy, which was sold to Kesko Oy </p>
<p>in May 1996, Sponsor said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +35 89 6805 0245</p>
</text>
